    <text>
        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="lzh" xml:space="preserve">
<ab>
<lb n="01"/>
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a15"/><persName>文殊 師利 文殊師利 文殊</persName>白<persName>佛</persName>言：“<persName>世 尊</persName>！何以故名般
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a16"/>若
<lb n="02"/>波羅蜜？”<persName>佛</persName>言：“般若波羅蜜，無邊、無際，
<lb n="03"/>無名、
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a17"/>無相，非思量、无歸依、無洲渚，無
<lb n="04"/>犯、無福，無晦、
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a18"/>無朙，如猶如法界無有分亝，
<lb n="05"/>亦無限數，是名般
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a19"/>若波羅蜜，亦名菩
<lb n="06"/>薩摩訶薩行處。非行處、非不
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a20"/>行處，悉入
<lb n="07"/>一乗，名非行處。何以故？無念無作
<lb n="T08n0232_0731a21"/>故。”
</ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus"/>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                <p>Mañjuśrī addressed the Buddha, saying, “ World-Honored One , why is it named prajñāpāramitā ?” The Buddha said: “ Prajñāpāramitā is without boundary, without bourn; without name, without attributes; inconceivable, without refuge, without sandbank; without sin, without merit; without obscurity, without illumination. Like the Realm of the Law it is without demarcation and also limitless in number. This is named prajñāpāramitā . It is also named the Site of Bodhisattva-Mahāsattva Practice. Since it is neither a site of practice nor of non-practice — all [Sites of Bodhisattva-Mahāsattva Practice] belonging to the One Vehicle — it is named the Site of Non-Practice. Why is this? Because it is unthought and unconditioned.”</p>
            </div>
        </body>
